7. WHY 1P1 CANNOT BE WRITTEN AT ALL, AND WHY 3P1 IS NOT A RESERVOIR
-------------------------------------------------------------------
  Ar valence = 8 electrons. With p3 (6 in lone pairs) and no bonds, charge neutrality
  forces u = 2: `Ar u2 p3 c0` is the ONLY neutral bond-free p3 adjacency list, and it
  is a TRIPLET (multiplicity 3). The singlet 1s2 (1P1) therefore has no adjacency list
  in RMG at all -- it is not an option this entry declines, it is unrepresentable.

  Radiative rates, NIST ASD ver. 5.12 (lines 104-108 nm, both from the ground state):
    1s2 (1P1) -> ground  104.8220 nm  A = 5.32e+08 s^-1  -> tau = 1.88 ns
    1s4 (3P1) -> ground  106.6660 nm  A = 1.320e+08 s^-1 -> tau = 7.58 ns
  Against the metastables:
    1s5 (3P2)  tau = 38 (+8/-5) s   measured, Katori & Shimizu, PRL 70 (1993) 3545
    1s5 (3P2)  tau = 55.9 s         computed, Small-Warren & Chiu, PRA 11 (1975) 1777
    1s3 (3P0)  tau = 44.9 s         computed, Small-Warren & Chiu, PRA 11 (1975) 1777
  Ratio 3P2 : 3P1 lifetime = 5.02e+09 -- nine to ten orders of magnitude.
